  "sections": [
    {
      "title": "Core decisions",
      "level": 2,
      "scope": "locale",
      "intro": "",
      "columns": {
        "en": 0,
        "target": 1,
        "use": 2,
        "notes": 3
      },
      "terms": [
        {
          "en": "programming / coding",
          "target": "programació",
          "use": "ca",
          "anchor": "term-programming-coding"
        },
        {
          "en": "developer",
          "target": "desenvolupador",
          "use": "ca",
          "notes": "Masculine generic default in flowing prose; see guide § Style notes.",
          "anchor": "term-developer"
        },
        {
          "en": "streak",
          "target": "ratxa",
          "use": "ca",
          "notes": "Standard Catalan word for a run/streak (sports, games, daily habits). Medium confidence; single-source, flag for native-speaker confirmation on first real use.",
          "anchor": "term-streak"
        },
        {
          "en": "tech / tech industry",
          "target": "sector tecnològic",
          "use": "ca",
          "notes": "Prose form; use plain \"tecnologia\" for the general field.",
          "anchor": "term-tech-tech-industry"
        },
        {
          "en": "pitfall",
          "target": "parany",
          "use": "ca",
          "notes": "Literally \"trap\"; closest natural fit for \"a mistake to watch out for.\" Medium confidence, flag for review.",
          "anchor": "term-pitfall"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Values & data types",
      "level": 3,
      "scope": "locale",
      "intro": "",
      "columns": {
        "en": 0,
        "target": 1,
        "use": 2,
        "notes": 3
      },
      "terms": [
        {
          "en": "value",
          "target": "valor",
          "use": "ca",
          "notes": "Ordinary word.",
          "anchor": "term-value"
        },
        {
          "en": "number",
          "target": "nombre",
          "use": "ca",
          "notes": "Ordinary word.",
          "anchor": "term-number"
        },
        {
          "en": "true / false",
          "target": "cert / fals",
          "use": "ca",
          "notes": "Medium confidence; not independently cross-verified, flag for review on first real use.",
          "anchor": "term-true-false"
        },
        {
          "en": "character",
          "target": "caràcter",
          "use": "ca",
          "anchor": "term-character"
        },
        {
          "en": "integer",
          "target": "nombre enter",
          "use": "ca",
          "anchor": "term-integer"
        },
        {
          "en": "float / decimal",
          "target": "nombre decimal",
          "use": "ca",
          "notes": "TERMCAT also has _nombre de coma flotant_ for the floating-point representation specifically; use the simpler _decimal_ form for learner-facing prose.",
          "anchor": "term-float-decimal"
        },
        {
          "en": "data type",
          "target": "tipus de dades",
          "use": "ca",
          "anchor": "term-data-type"
        },
        {
          "en": "array / list",
          "target": "llista",
          "use": "ca",
          "notes": "Real Catalan CS usage (UPC OCW, Jutge.org) distinguishes _vector_/_taula_ (fixed array), _llista_ (Python-style dynamic list), and _matriu_ (2-D matrix, a different concept). Recommend _llista_ as Jiki's single array/list term since it avoids the matrix collision.",
          "anchor": "term-array-list"
        },
        {
          "en": "string",
          "target": "cadena de caràcters",
          "use": "ca",
          "notes": "Use the full form where the source `<define>`s it, then _cadena_ alone. Confirmed by TERMCAT and by direct textbook usage (chapter title \"Cadenes de caràcters\").",
          "anchor": "term-string"
        },
        {
          "en": "Boolean",
          "target": "booleà",
          "use": "ca",
          "notes": "Unlike some languages, Catalan fully localizes this; no need to keep \"Boolean\" in English.",
          "anchor": "term-boolean"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Functions & control flow",
      "level": 3,
      "scope": "locale",
      "intro": "",
